"CFBundleDisplayName" = "سَرى البارق";
"NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription" = "سَرى البارق shows your position on the outing map and shares it automatically with the members of the outing you joined, only while it is running. Sharing stops when you leave the outing or it ends.";
"NSMicrophoneUsageDescription" = "Picks up your voice only while you hold \"Push to talk\" and sends it live to the outing's members, like a walkie-talkie. For members on an older version a short clip is sent instead and deleted from the server after 10 minutes; nothing is saved on your phone. When you tap the mic in search it only listens for the place you say.";
"NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription" = "When you tap the mic in \"Where to?\" we turn the place you say into search text, on your phone when possible. Your voice is not saved.";
"NSCameraUsageDescription" = "The camera is used to scan a QR code (an outing invite or your recovery code) and to take a photo of a point you choose to share with the outing's members. Photos are not saved to your library.";
"NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription" = "While you are a member of a running outing, سَرى البارق keeps sharing your live position with that outing's members only, in the background and with the screen locked (the blue location indicator shows), until you leave or the outing ends. It also records your trail even when the screen is locked, so \"Way back\" can lead you out the way you came; the trail stays on this phone and is never sent to your friends or our servers (stretches of it are matched to streets via Mapbox only).";
"NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription" = "When the internet drops, سَرى البارق connects directly to nearby phones of your outing's members (Bluetooth and peer-to-peer Wi-Fi) to exchange encrypted positions and alerts, and only while you are sharing your location.";
"NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription" = "Saves the trip story (an image or video made on your phone) to Photos only when you tap Save to Photos. The app never reads your photos.";

/* Precise Location is off: temporary full accuracy for the trail. */
"TrailRecording" = "Precise Location is off, so your trail would be kilometres off. Allow precise location for this outing so your trail follows the exact streets you drove and \"Way back\" can lead you the same way.";
